- launchConversion.py

Launch in serial launchConversion.py after sourcing FSDM and Cassiopeée.
It will read the meshes in the directory InitialMeshes_wSolution, convert them in CGNS-NGon format
and compare them with the reference meshes stored in the directory Data/.
If a difference is detected, the script will throw an error and will stop.

- launchCheckSurfaceAndBoundaryCoefficients.py

The test performed launching the script launchCheckSurfaceAndBoundaryCoefficients.py
is an additional test, which is useless if the launchConversion.py succeeds.
It should be used to verify that, despite a minor difference in the .cgns files
(for example the name of a zone/node/BC, a different NGON norm, etc ), the mesh remains formally identical.
It must be executed after launchConversion.py, because it uses the information in the directory Data/.
CODA should be sourced in this case, additionally to FSDM and Cassiopée.

